@* ===== Home: intro + 6 featured destinations ===== *@
<section class="section" id="featured">
    <div class="container">
        <div class="section-head section-head--center">
            <span class="eyebrow">Start here</span>
            <h2>Six places to see first</h2>
            <p class="lead">
                Armenia is small enough to cross in a day but deep enough to fill a lifetime.
                These six stops give a first-time visitor the country's essentials: the capital,
                a pagan temple, rock-cut monasteries, a mountain lake, and the view of Mount Ararat.
            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card-grid">
            <article class="card">
                <figure><img src="~/images/yerevan-700.webp"
                         srcset="/images/yerevan-700.webp 700w, /images/yerevan-1400.webp 1400w"
                         sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 351px, (min-width: 768px) 46vw, 92vw"
                         width="1584" height="990" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                         alt="Republic Square and the pink tuff buildings of central Yerevan" /></figure>
                <div class="card__body">
                    <span class="card__region">Capital</span>
                    <h3>Yerevan</h3>
                    <p>Pink-stone boulevards, Republic Square, the Cascade steps and a café culture that runs late into the night.</p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <article class="card">
                <figure><img src="~/images/garni-700.webp"
                         srcset="/images/garni-700.webp 700w, /images/garni-1400.webp 1400w"
                         sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 351px, (min-width: 768px) 46vw, 92vw"
                         width="1584" height="990" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                         alt="The colonnaded Greco-Roman temple of Garni above the Azat gorge" /></figure>
                <div class="card__body">
                    <span class="card__region">Kotayk</span>
                    <h3>Garni Temple</h3>
                    <p>A 1st-century Greco-Roman temple — the only standing colonnaded temple of its kind in the region.</p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <article class="card">
                <figure><img src="~/images/geghard-700.webp"
                         srcset="/images/geghard-700.webp 700w, /images/geghard-1400.webp 1400w"
                         sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 351px, (min-width: 768px) 46vw, 92vw"
                         width="1584" height="990" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                         alt="Geghard Monastery carved into the cliffs of the Azat valley" /></figure>
                <div class="card__body">
                    <span class="card__region">Kotayk · UNESCO</span>
                    <h3>Geghard Monastery</h3>
                    <p>A medieval monastery partly carved straight out of the mountain, with chapels that sing with natural acoustics.</p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <article class="card">
                <figure><img src="~/images/sevan-700.webp"
                         srcset="/images/sevan-700.webp 700w, /images/sevan-1400.webp 1400w"
                         sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 351px, (min-width: 768px) 46vw, 92vw"
                         width="1584" height="990" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                         alt="Sevanavank monastery on a peninsula above the blue waters of Lake Sevan" /></figure>
                <div class="card__body">
                    <span class="card__region">Gegharkunik</span>
                    <h3>Lake Sevan</h3>
                    <p>A vast high-altitude lake at about 1,900 m, with the Sevanavank monastery on its peninsula and beaches in summer.</p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <article class="card">
                <figure><img src="~/images/tatev-700.webp"
                         srcset="/images/tatev-700.webp 700w, /images/tatev-1400.webp 1400w"
                         sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 351px, (min-width: 768px) 46vw, 92vw"
                         width="1584" height="990" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                         alt="Tatev Monastery on the edge of the Vorotan gorge with the cable car approaching" /></figure>
                <div class="card__body">
                    <span class="card__region">Syunik</span>
                    <h3>Tatev Monastery</h3>
                    <p>A 9th-century monastery perched over the Vorotan gorge, reached by the record-setting Wings of Tatev cableway.</p>
                </div>
            </article>

            <article class="card">
                <figure><img src="~/images/khor-virap-700.webp"
                         srcset="/images/khor-virap-700.webp 700w, /images/khor-virap-1400.webp 1400w"
                         sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 351px, (min-width: 768px) 46vw, 92vw"
                         width="1584" height="990" loading="lazy" decoding="async"
                         alt="Khor Virap monastery with snow-capped Mount Ararat behind it" /></figure>
                <div class="card__body">
                    <span class="card__region">Ararat</span>
                    <h3>Khor Virap</h3>
                    <p>The classic postcard: a hilltop monastery framed by Mount Ararat, and the pit where St Gregory the Illuminator was imprisoned.</p>
                </div>
            </article>
        </div>

        <p class="section-foot">
            <a class="btn btn--outline" href="#destinations">See all destinations</a>
        </p>
    </div>
</section>
